Dear Vincent,
my name is Francesco and I am a PhD student at the University of Granada.
I am working with GGIR (version: 2.8.2) to analyze data retrieved from Geneactiv devices.
We collected data for 10 days (50 Hz of frequency) from participants working on a ship.
They have an unusual sleep pattern (e.g., they can take several naps, or the principal sleeping time can start very late in the night).
When I generate the outputs there is an issue with the activity graphs included in the report(no result on the histogram, and a lot of inactivity on the daily analysis). I do not know if it depends on the thresholds or maybe some mistake in the code.
Moreover, I would like to obtain the number of naps and duration for each day. Could it be possible? (I tried with the advanced sleep log but it does not work well).
Last thing: I would like to obtain a graph like in the attached figure (Report example colors). Should I change something in the code to obtain it?

Thanks in advance for your help!
Best regards,
Francesco

g.shell.GGIR(###########
             #General parameters
             ###########
             mode=mode1,
             datadir=datadir1,
             outputdir=outputdir1,
             studyname=studyname1,
             f0=f0,
             f1=f1,
             overwrite=TRUE, #overwrite previous milestone data
             do.imp=TRUE, #do imputation (recommended)
             idloc=1, #idlocation (1=file header, 2 = filename)
             print.filename=TRUE,
             storefolderstructure=FALSE,
             #############
             #Part 1
             #############
             #Function : reading file, auto-calibration, and extracting features
             windowsizes = c(5,900,3600), #epoch lenght, non-wear detection resolution, non-wear detection evaluation window
             do.cal=TRUE, #Apply autocalibration
             do.enmo=TRUE, #needed for physical activity analysis
             do.anglez=TRUE, #needed for sleep detection
             chunksize=1, #size of data chuncks to be read (1 is maximum)
             printsummary=TRUE,
             ############
             #Part 2
             ############
             #Function: non-wear detection, imputation, and basic descriptives
             strategy = 1, #srtategy type (see manual)
             ndaywindows = 10, #only relevant if strategy = 3
             hrs.del.start = 0, #only relevant if strategy = 2, how many HOURS need to be ignored at the start of the measurement
             hrs.del.end = 0, #only relevant if strategy = 2, How many hours need to be ignored at the end of the measurement
             maxdur = 10, #how many days of measurements do you maximum expect?
             includedaycrit = 16, #number of minimum valid hours in a day to attempt physical activity analysis (default is 16)
             M5L5res = 10, #resolution in minutes of M5 and L5 calculation
             winhr = c(5,10), #size of M5 and L5 (5 hours by default)
             qlevels = c(c(1380/1440),c(1410/1440)), #quantiles to calculate, set value at c() if you do not want quantiles
             qwindow=c(0,8,21,24), #window over which to calculate quantile
             ilevels=c(0,100,400,8000), #acceleration values
             iglevels=TRUE,
             mvpathreshold = c(100), #MVPA (moderate and vigorous physical activity threshold)
             bout.metric = 6,
             ################
             #Part 3
             ################
             #Function:Sleep detection
             anglethreshold=5,
             timethreshold=5,
             ignorenonwear = TRUE, #if true ignore detected monitor non-wear periods in the detection of sustained inactivity bouts to avoid confusion between monitor non-wear time
             do.part3.pdf=TRUE,
             ###############
             #Part 4
             ###############
             #function: integrating sleeplog with sleep detection, storing day and person specific summaries
             excludefirstlast=FALSE, #exclude first and last night for sleep analysis?
             includenightcrit = 2, # number of minimum valid hours in a day to attempt sleep analysis (default is 16)
             def.noc.sleep = 1, #1 if you use sleep log
             loglocation = "E:/ActigraphArmada_sleeplog_1/Sleeplog/050469.csv",
             outliers.only = FALSE,
             criterror = 4,
             relyonguider = TRUE,
             sleeplogidnum = TRUE, #is the participant in the sleeplog stored as a number (TRUE) or as a character (FALSE)
             colid=1, #column in which the participant ID is stored
             coln1=2, #column number for the first day
             do.visual=TRUE,
             nnights = 9, #number of nights in the sleeplog
             #########################
             #Part 5
             #########################
             #function: merging physical activity with sleep analysis
             excludefirstlast.part5=FALSE,
             save_ms5rawlevels=FALSE,
             threshold.lig=c(20), #threshold for inactivity (can be more than one number)
             threshold.mod=c(69), #threshold for moderate activity (can be more than one number)
             threshold.vig=c(100), #threshold for vigorous activity (can be more than one number)
             boutcrit = 0.9,
             boutcrit.in <http://boutcrit.in> = 0.9, #fraction of inactivity bout that needs to be below the threshold
             boutcriter.lig = 0.8, #fraction of light activity bout that needs to be between the threshold
             boutcriter.mvpa = 0.9, #fraction of light activity bout that needs to be above the threshold
             boutdur.in <http://boutdur.in> = c(10,20,30), #duration of bouts to be calculated
             boutdur.lig = c(1,5,10), #duration of bouts to be calculated
             boutdur.mvpa = c(1,5,10), #duration of bouts to be calculated
             timewindow=c("MM"),
             ################
             #Report generation
             ################
             #function: generating reports based on meta-data
             do.report=c(2,4,5), #for what parts does and report need to be generated?
             visualreport=TRUE,
             dofirstpage=TRUE, #first page of pdf-report with simple summary histograms
             viewingwindow=1) #window of visual report: 1 centres at day and 2 centres at night

