Dear Dan,

> I am trying to process the NHANES accelerometry data sets using GGIR

​Can you specify which NHANES accelerometry data set, as many have been released over the years. GGIR has been tested with standard ActiGraph output and not custom unique file formats generated for specific studies. If I am not mistaken the latest NHANES data comes with custom file formats. So, if that is the case then it may be good to better understand how this differs from the standard formats.

Which GGIR version are you working with? In the latest CRAN version we made some enhancements to handle the specific nature of Actigraph files with idle sleep. Although, that would of course only work with standard ActiGraph file formats.

Are you trying to process the csv file or the gt3x file? If csv, can you process the gt3x file?

Thanks, Vincent

